  "legalPrivacyDataTitle": "Where your data lives",
  "legalPrivacyDataBody": "Matheasy keeps your progress, achievements, learning preferences and settings on this device. When you sign in with Google or Apple, that learning data is also synced to your account over a secure connection (using Google Firebase), so it is backed up and follows you to a new device.",
  "legalPrivacyCollectTitle": "What we collect",
  "legalPrivacyCollectBody": "Signing in with Google or Apple gives us a basic profile — your name, email address and photo — to create and personalise your account. To run the app we process the problems you scan or type, your practice activity and your progress. For signed-in users this is stored in your account so it can sync across your devices. We don't ask for anything else.",
  "legalPrivacyAiTitle": "AI processing (OpenAI)",
  "legalPrivacyAiBody": "Matheasy is powered by AI. When you scan a problem, type an equation, ask the AI tutor or open Visual Learning, that content — the photo of your work, the equation text, or your question — is sent over a secure connection to our AI provider, OpenAI, so it can read the problem and generate the solution, explanation or reply. Photos are screened automatically for unsafe content first. This content is used to answer you; it is never sold, and it is never used to target advertising. OpenAI's handling of it is governed by their API data-usage policies.",
  "legalPrivacyAdsTitle": "Advertising and measurement (Meta)",
  "legalPrivacyAdsBody": "We advertise Matheasy on Meta platforms such as Facebook and Instagram, and we use Meta's software kit to measure whether those ads actually work. If you allow tracking, we share app activity with Meta: that you installed and opened Matheasy, created an account, finished onboarding, ran your first scan, opened the AI tutor or Visual Learning, started or completed practice, and saw the upgrade screen. Subscription events are sent to Meta by our servers rather than by the app. Alongside these we share your device's advertising identifier and an account identifier, which Meta uses to match you to an ad you may have seen. Meta may use this data to measure and target advertising, including on its own platforms.",
  "legalPrivacyAdsChoiceTitle": "Your choice about tracking",
  "legalPrivacyAdsChoiceBody": "Nothing above happens unless you agree to it. We ask your age first, then ask your permission. If you decline — or if you tell us you are under 13 — the Meta kit is never activated: no advertising identifier is collected and no app activity is sent to Meta at all. Matheasy works exactly the same either way; no feature is withheld for saying no. You can change your mind at any time in your device settings, under Privacy & Security → Tracking.",
  "legalPrivacyAnalyticsTitle": "Analytics and crash reports",
  "legalPrivacyAnalyticsBody": "We use Google Firebase to understand which parts of the app get used and to receive automatic crash reports, so we can fix what breaks and decide what to build next. This is tied to your app installation rather than to your advertising profile, and it is never sold.",
  "legalPrivacyChildrenTitle": "Children's privacy",
  "legalPrivacyChildrenBody": "Matheasy is built for learners of every age, including students under 13, and every feature is available to them. What changes is tracking: we ask your age before any advertising software is allowed to run, and for under-13 learners the Meta kit is never activated, no advertising identifier is collected, and nothing is shared for ad targeting. Beyond the account details described above, we do not knowingly collect personal information from a child. If you believe a child has provided more than that, contact us and we will delete it.",
  "legalPrivacyControlTitle": "You are in control",
  "legalPrivacyControlBody": "You can edit or clear your learning preferences at any time. Deleting your account permanently removes your synced learning data from our servers along with the copy on this device — we'll ask you to sign in once more first, to prove the account is yours. You can withdraw tracking permission whenever you like from your device settings.",
  "legalPrivacyContactTitle": "Contact us",
  "legalPrivacyContactBody": "Questions about this policy, or want your data deleted? Email us at {email} and we'll help.",
